IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aca-dates`
IMPORT `aca-amounts`

-- Accident Compensation Act 1985 (Vic) -- suing for damages for a work injury before 1 July 2014: which section governs
-- (ss 134A, 134AB, 135A), the serious injury gateway and its time limits, the thresholds and maximums, the reductions, the
-- costs rules, and what the damages do to compensation.
--
-- SEAT: the injured worker. Every exported question is one the worker would ask: "Which section decides whether I can sue?",
-- "May I make my serious injury application now?", "Am I deemed to have a serious injury?", "By when must WorkSafe answer?",
-- "By when must I apply to the court?", "What may I sue for?", "Do I meet the loss of earning capacity test?", "What can the
-- court award me?", "Who pays the costs?", "Do my weekly payments stop?". The Authority (WorkSafe), self-insurers and the
-- court get no seat: their decisions (satisfied, a certificate, leave) are asked as facts.
--
-- Provisions: s 4(1)(a); s 134A(1), (3); s 134AA (transport accidents, as a fact); s 134AB(1)-(4A), (6), (6A), (7), (9),
-- (12)-(17), (20), (20A), (21), (21A), (22), (25), (26), (28), (28A), (32), (36), (36A), (36B), (37), (38)(e)-(g); s 134ABA
-- (noted); s 135A(1)-(2D), (2DB), (2DE), (3), (4), (6A), (6B), (7), (11)-(13A), (14), (18), (18AA), (18AB), (19); s 135AC.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("shall not ... except", "may
-- not ... unless", "must not ... unless", "may only ... after"), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given;
-- each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Accident
-- Compensation Act 1985, Version No. 237 (2 October 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Damages for a work injury before 1 July 2014 (Part IV Divisions 8A and 9)`

§§ `Which section decides whether I can sue my employer`

-- s 4(1)(a): the Act applies "to and in relation to an injury to a worker on or after the appointed day but before 1 July
-- 2014". (The appointed day is 4 p.m. on 31 August 1985 (s 5(1) and the heading of Division 3A Subdivision 2); an injury
-- before 1 September 1985 is taken as before it.)
-- s 135A(1): "employment before 12 November 1997". s 134A(1): "employment on or after 12 November 1997 but before 20
-- October 1999 shall not, in proceedings commenced in respect of the injury or otherwise, recover any damages of any kind";
-- s 134A(3): except "if -- (a) the injury is a condition that is -- (i) a dust-related condition ...; or (ii) an eligible
-- progressive disease attributable or related to exposure to occupational dust; and (b) the employment was a significant
-- contributing factor", in accordance with Division 8A (s 134AB(2A)). s 134AB(1): "employment on or after 20 October 1999
-- but before 1 July 2014".
-- Transport accidents (s 134AA(a), s 134AB(1)(a)(i), s 135A(1)(a)(i)) go by the Transport Accident Act 1986: NOTHING here.
DECLARE `Damages route` IS ONE OF
    `section 135A, for employment before 12 November 1997`
    `no damages of any kind, under section 134A(1)`
    `section 134AB, through section 134AB(2A), for a dust condition`
    `section 134AB, for employment from 20 October 1999 to 30 June 2014`

GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `my injury is a dust condition to which employment significantly contributed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my injury arose out of a transport accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Damages route`
`the damages route for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `dust` `my injury is a dust condition to which employment significantly contributed` `transport` `my injury arose out of a transport accident` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my injury arose out of a transport accident` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the Transport Accident Act 1986 governs)
           IF `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 1 9 1985) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 4(1)(b), before the appointed day)
           IF `the day of the injury` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2014) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 4(1)(a); the 2013 Act governs)
           IF `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 12 11 1997) THEN JUST `section 135A, for employment before 12 November 1997`
           IF `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 20 10 1999) THEN `the 1997-1999 route`
           OTHERWISE JUST `section 134AB, for employment from 20 October 1999 to 30 June 2014`
    WHERE
        `the 1997-1999 route` MEANS
            IF `my injury is a dust condition to which employment significantly contributed`
            THEN JUST `section 134AB, through section 134AB(2A), for a dust condition`
            ELSE JUST `no damages of any kind, under section 134A(1)`

@export Which section of the Accident Compensation Act 1985 decides whether I can sue for damages for my work injury (ss 134A, 134AB, 135A)?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of your injury, from the employment it arose out of or in the course of
      `my injury is a dust condition to which employment significantly contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury is a dust-related condition, or a progressive disease from exposure to occupational dust, to which the employment was a significant contributing factor
      `my injury arose out of a transport accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury arose out of a transport accident (a road or rail accident under the Transport Accident Act 1986)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Damages route`
`Which section decides whether I can sue for damages` MEANS
    `the damages route for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `dust` `my injury is a dust condition to which employment significantly contributed` `transport` `my injury arose out of a transport accident`

§ `Section 134AB -- injuries from 20 October 1999 to 30 June 2014`

§§ `s 134AB(15) -- an impairment of 30% or more`

-- s 134AB(15): "If the assessment under section 104B made before an application under subsection (4) is made of the degree
-- of impairment of the worker as a result of the injury is 30 per centum or more, the injury is deemed to be a serious injury
-- within the meaning of this section." The "if" fails: JUST FALSE (deemed by this route; the injury may still be serious).
@export Is my injury deemed a serious injury because my impairment was assessed at 30% or more (s 134AB(15))?
GIVEN `an assessment under s 104B was made before my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your degree of impairment was assessed under s 104B before you made your serious injury application under s 134AB(4)
      `my assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree of impairment from that assessment, in per cent
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my injury deemed serious by its impairment` MEANS
    JUST (`an assessment under s 104B was made before my application` AND `my assessed degree of impairment` AT LEAST 30)

§§ `s 134AB(3), (4), (4A), (21) -- may I make my serious injury application now`

-- s 134AB(3): no proceedings "unless -- (a) determinations of the degree of impairment of the worker have been made under
-- section 104B and the worker has made an application under subsection (4); or (b) subject to any directions issued under
-- section 134AF, the worker elects to make an application under subsection (4) on the ground that the worker has a serious
-- injury". (4): "a worker may only make an application -- (a) if subsection (3)(a) applies, after the worker -- (i) has
-- advised the Authority or self-insurer under section 104B(6B) or 104B(7B) that he or she accepts the determinations of
-- degree of impairment; or (ii) has received the advice of the Authority or self-insurer under section 104B(10); or (b) if
-- subsection (3)(b) applies -- (i) after a period of at least 18 months has elapsed since the event or circumstance giving
-- rise to the injury occurred". (4A): "If a worker has made a claim for compensation under section 98C in respect of an
-- injury, the worker must not make an application under subsection (4) ... unless -- (a) the degree of impairment ... has
-- been determined in accordance with section 104B; and (b) the worker has accepted the determination of the degree of
-- impairment; and (c) the worker has accepted the entitlement to compensation." (21): "the worker must not make a further
-- application under that subsection in respect of that injury."
-- s 134AF(1A): the Minister's directions may limit the cases in which an election can be made: asked.
-- s 134AB(4)(b)(ii) (an application under the pre-2004 s 104B) is not encoded.
DECLARE `Application route` IS ONE OF
    `after determinations of my impairment under s 104B`
    `by electing to apply on the ground that I have a serious injury`

-- 18 months after a day: the same day of the month, a year and six months on (a day that does not exist rolls forward).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`eighteen months after` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT MOST 6
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS 6) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 6) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 2)

GIVEN `the route` IS AN `Application route`
      `I have made a serious injury application for this injury before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have accepted the determinations or received the s 104B(10) advice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister's directions allow my election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the event giving rise to the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day I would apply` IS A DATE
      `I have claimed under s 98C for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my impairment was determined under s 104B and I accepted it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I accepted the entitlement to compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`I may make a serious injury application` `the route` `before` `I have made a serious injury application for this injury before` `accepted` `I have accepted the determinations or received the s 104B(10) advice` `directions` `the Minister's directions allow my election` `event` `the day of the event giving rise to the injury` `applying on` `the day I would apply` `s 98C claim` `I have claimed under s 98C for this injury` `determined and accepted` `my impairment was determined under s 104B and I accepted it` `entitlement accepted` `I accepted the entitlement to compensation` MEANS
    IF `I have made a serious injury application for this injury before`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `I have claimed under s 98C for this injury` AND (NOT (`my impairment was determined under s 104B and I accepted it` AND `I accepted the entitlement to compensation`))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST `the route allows it`
    WHERE
        `the route allows it` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the route`
            WHEN `after determinations of my impairment under s 104B` THEN `I have accepted the determinations or received the s 104B(10) advice`
            WHEN `by electing to apply on the ground that I have a serious injury` THEN
                `the Minister's directions allow my election` AND (`the day I would apply` `is on or after` (`eighteen months after` `the day of the event giving rise to the injury`))

@export May I make my serious injury application under s 134AB(4) now (s 134AB(3), (4), (4A), (21))?
GIVEN `the route` IS AN `Application route` @desc How you would apply: after determinations of your impairment under s 104B, or by electing to apply on the ground that you have a serious injury
      `I have made a serious injury application for this injury before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already made a serious injury application under s 134AB(4) for this injury
      `I have accepted the determinations or received the s 104B(10) advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the first route: whether you have told WorkSafe or the self-insurer you accept its impairment determinations, or received its advice under s 104B(10)
      `the Minister's directions allow my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the second route: whether the Minister's directions under s 134AF allow an election in a case like yours
      `the day of the event giving rise to the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the event or circumstance that gave rise to your injury
      `the day I would apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make the application
      `I have claimed under s 98C for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have claimed a lump sum for non-economic loss under s 98C for this injury
      `my impairment was determined under s 104B and I accepted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have claimed under s 98C: whether your degree of impairment has been determined under s 104B and you accepted that determination
      `I accepted the entitlement to compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have claimed under s 98C: whether you have accepted the entitlement to that compensation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I make my serious injury application now` MEANS
    `I may make a serious injury application` `the route` `before` `I have made a serious injury application for this injury before` `accepted` `I have accepted the determinations or received the s 104B(10) advice` `directions` `the Minister's directions allow my election` `event` `the day of the event giving rise to the injury` `applying on` `the day I would apply` `s 98C claim` `I have claimed under s 98C for this injury` `determined and accepted` `my impairment was determined under s 104B and I accepted it` `entitlement accepted` `I accepted the entitlement to compensation`

§§ `s 134AB(7), (9) and s 135A(2D), (2DB) -- WorkSafe's duty to answer, and a deemed serious injury`

DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF
    `the worker`
    `the Authority or self-insurer`

DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF
    `advise the worker in writing on the serious injury application`
    `advise the worker in writing of the impairment determination or the refusal to make one`

-- s 134AB(7): "The Authority or self-insurer must, within 120 days (or such other period as may be specified in directions
-- made under section 134AF) of receiving the application, advise the worker in writing -- (a) that the worker is deemed to
-- have a serious injury; or (b) if the worker is not deemed to have a serious injury, whether or not the Authority or
-- self-insurer will issue a certificate under subsection (16)(a)." (9): "If the Authority or self-insurer fails to advise the
-- worker in writing within the period ... the worker is deemed to have suffered a serious injury."
-- The period is counted leaving out 24 December to 9 January (s 134AB(6A)) and the days of a refused or hindered medical
-- examination (s 134AB(6)): the rule runs on the count, from the day the application was received.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 134AB(7) -- the Authority or self-insurer must advise the worker within the days allowed` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Authority or self-insurer`
    MUST `advise the worker in writing on the serious injury application`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Authority or self-insurer` BECAUSE "no written advice within the period: the worker is deemed to have suffered a serious injury (s 134AB(9))"

-- s 135A(2D): "The Authority or self-insurer must, within 120 days of receiving the application, advise the worker in
-- writing -- (a) of the determination; or (b) of the refusal to make a determination under subsection (2C)." (2DB): if it
-- fails, "the worker is deemed to have suffered a serious injury". (2AA): 210 days for an application received "after 10
-- August 2000 but before 1 September 2000". (2BB): the days of a refused or hindered medical examination are disregarded.
-- Plain days: s 135A has no Christmas rule.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 135A(2D) -- the Authority or self-insurer must advise the worker within the days allowed` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Authority or self-insurer`
    MUST `advise the worker in writing of the impairment determination or the refusal to make one`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Authority or self-insurer` BECAUSE "no written advice within 120 days: the worker is deemed to have suffered a serious injury (s 135A(2DB))"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened (as in the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding, gva-seat.l4). On the stable
-- l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH; so where the advice was given, FULFILLED means in time
-- and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether advice given now would still be in time. It takes a
-- DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `the duty was kept`
    `the duty was not kept`
    `the duty is still open`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
      `the act` IS A `Claim act`
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done` IS A NUMBER
      `the time now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of` `the rule` `with` `the act` `done` `the act has been done` `at` `the time the act was done` `now` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the Authority or self-insurer` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty was kept`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the Authority or self-insurer` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty is still open`
         OTHERWISE `the duty was not kept`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A `What became of the duty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`deemed serious, if` `the outcome` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `the duty was not kept` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 134AB(9): deemed, on the s 134AB(6A) count. The "if ... fails" does not hold: JUST FALSE. Directions under s 134AF
-- that set another period: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the day the application was received` IS A DATE
      `WorkSafe has advised me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the advice` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the days disregarded under s 134AB(6)` IS A NUMBER
      `directions set another period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`I am deemed to have a serious injury under s 134AB(9), received` `the day the application was received` `advised` `WorkSafe has advised me` `on` `the day of the advice` `as of` `today` `disregarded` `the days disregarded under s 134AB(6)` `directions` `directions set another period` MEANS
    IF `directions set another period`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the period in the Minister's directions)
    ELSE JUST (`deemed serious, if` (`what became of` (`s 134AB(7) -- the Authority or self-insurer must advise the worker within the days allowed` 120) `with` `advise the worker in writing on the serious injury application` `done` `WorkSafe has advised me` `at` (`counted` `the day of the advice`) `now` (`counted` `today`)))
    WHERE
        GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `counted` `the day` MEANS max 0 ((`the counted days from` `the day the application was received` `to` `the day`) MINUS `the days disregarded under s 134AB(6)`)

@export Am I deemed to have a serious injury because WorkSafe or the self-insurer did not answer my application in time (s 134AB(7), (9))?
GIVEN `the day the application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer received your serious injury application under s 134AB(4)
      `WorkSafe has advised me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer has advised you in writing on the application
      `the day of the advice` IS A DATE @desc The day of that written advice (any day if there has been none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `the days disregarded under s 134AB(6)` IS A NUMBER @desc Days that do not count because you unreasonably refused or hindered a requested medical examination: the days from the refusal to the examination, leaving out 24 December to 9 January (0 if none)
      `directions set another period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister's directions under s 134AF set a period other than 120 days for your application
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I deemed to have a serious injury because the answer was late` MEANS
    `I am deemed to have a serious injury under s 134AB(9), received` `the day the application was received` `advised` `WorkSafe has advised me` `on` `the day of the advice` `as of` `today` `disregarded` `the days disregarded under s 134AB(6)` `directions` `directions set another period`

@export By when must WorkSafe or the self-insurer answer my serious injury application (s 134AB(6), (6A), (7))?
GIVEN `the day the application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer received your serious injury application under s 134AB(4)
      `the days disregarded under s 134AB(6)` IS A NUMBER @desc Days that do not count because you unreasonably refused or hindered a requested medical examination, leaving out 24 December to 9 January (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my serious injury application be answered` MEANS
    `the date` (120 PLUS `the days disregarded under s 134AB(6)`) `counted days after` `the day the application was received`

§§ `s 134AB(16), (37) -- the dates after WorkSafe's answer`

-- s 134AB(16)(b): leave of a court "on the application of the worker made within 30 days after the worker received advice
-- under subsection (7) or, with the consent of the Authority under subsection (20), after that period". Counted leaving out
-- 24 December to 9 January (s 134AB(6A) names subsection (16)).
@export By when must I apply to the court for leave to sue, if my impairment is under 30% (s 134AB(16)(b), (6A))?
GIVEN `the day I received the advice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received WorkSafe's or the self-insurer's written advice under s 134AB(7)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for leave to sue` MEANS `the date` 30 `counted days after` `the day I received the advice`

-- s 134AB(37): "response date means the date on which the period of 28 days after the determination date expires".
-- READING (fork F9): the 28 days are plain days: s 134AB(6A) lists subsections (7), (10)-(14) and (16), not (37).
-- "determination date" (s 134AB(37)): the day the worker receives the (7) advice of a deemed serious injury (an impairment of
-- 30% or more), the day the injury is deemed under (9), the day a certificate is issued under (16)(a), the day the court
-- gives leave under (16)(b), or the day an appeal against that leave is determined: the worker states it.
@export What is my response date, from which the conference and the statutory offer run (s 134AB(37))?
GIVEN `my determination date` IS A DATE @desc Your determination date: the day you received advice that you are deemed to have a serious injury, the day you were deemed under s 134AB(9), the day a certificate was issued, or the day the court gave leave (or any appeal against it was decided)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is my response date` MEANS `the date` 28 `plain days after` `my determination date`

-- s 134AB(12)(a): a conference "within 21 days after the response date"; (b): a statutory offer "at that conference, or after
-- the conference begins but no later than 60 days after the response date"; (13): if none is made the Authority or
-- self-insurer "is deemed ... to have made, on the 60th day after the response date, a statutory offer of nothing".
@export By when must WorkSafe or the self-insurer make its statutory offer, after which it is taken to offer nothing (s 134AB(12)(b), (13))?
GIVEN `my response date` IS A DATE @desc Your response date (28 days after your determination date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the statutory offer be made` MEANS `the date` 60 `counted days after` `my response date`

§§ `s 134AB(12), (14), (20A) -- when I may start my court proceedings`

-- s 134AB(12): no proceedings "unless -- (a) the worker and the Authority or self-insurer hold, or begin, a conference within
-- 21 days after the response date; and (b) the Authority or self-insurer makes a statutory offer ...; and (c) if the worker
-- does not accept that statutory offer within 21 days after it is made, the worker, before the expiration of that period,
-- makes a statutory counter offer ...; and (d) the Authority or self-insurer does not accept that counter offer within 21
-- days after it is made; and (e) the proceedings are commenced not earlier than 21 days, and not more than 51 days, after the
-- counter offer is made or, if a counter offer is deemed to have been made under subsection (14), not more than 30 days
-- after the day on which the counter offer is deemed to have been made." (14): with no counter offer, the worker "is deemed
-- ... to have made, on the 21st day after the statutory offer was made, a statutory counter offer of the maximum".
-- (20A): the Authority may consent to proceedings "earlier than 21 days" or "later than 51 days, but no later than 81
-- days", if the defence is not prejudiced, or "later than 81 days" if the failure was not the worker's fault: asked.
-- All counted leaving out 24 December to 9 January (s 134AB(6A)).
-- READING (fork F10): after a deemed counter offer, (e) states only a last day; the earliest day is then the day after the
-- deemed counter offer.
-- "must not commence ... unless": JUST FALSE when the day is outside.
GIVEN `the day of the statutory offer` IS A DATE
      `I made a counter offer within 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of my counter offer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the counter offer counts as made, after an offer on` `the day of the statutory offer` `made` `I made a counter offer within 21 days` `on` `the day of my counter offer` MEANS
    IF `I made a counter offer within 21 days`
    THEN `the day of my counter offer`
    ELSE `the date` 21 `counted days after` `the day of the statutory offer`

GIVEN `the day of the statutory offer` IS A DATE
      `I made a counter offer within 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of my counter offer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for my proceedings, after an offer on` `the day of the statutory offer` `made` `I made a counter offer within 21 days` `on` `the day of my counter offer` MEANS
    IF `I made a counter offer within 21 days`
    THEN `the date` 51 `counted days after` `the day of my counter offer`
    ELSE `the date` 30 `counted days after` (`the date` 21 `counted days after` `the day of the statutory offer`)

GIVEN `a conference was held or begun within 21 days after the response date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the statutory offer` IS A DATE
      `I made a counter offer within 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of my counter offer` IS A DATE
      `the insurer accepted my counter offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority consented under s 134AB(20A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I would commence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`I may commence proceedings, conference` `a conference was held or begun within 21 days after the response date` `offer on` `the day of the statutory offer` `counter offer` `I made a counter offer within 21 days` `on` `the day of my counter offer` `accepted` `the insurer accepted my counter offer` `consent` `the Authority consented under s 134AB(20A)` `commencing on` `the day I would commence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the insurer accepted my counter offer` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the Authority consented under s 134AB(20A)` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF (NOT `a conference was held or begun within 21 days after the response date`) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST (`not too early` AND `not too late`)
    WHERE
        `the counter offer day` MEANS `the day the counter offer counts as made, after an offer on` `the day of the statutory offer` `made` `I made a counter offer within 21 days` `on` `the day of my counter offer`
        `not too early` MEANS
            IF `I made a counter offer within 21 days`
            THEN `the day I would commence` `is on or after` (`the date` 21 `counted days after` `the counter offer day`)
            ELSE NOT (`the day I would commence` `is before` (`the date` 1 `counted days after` `the counter offer day`))
        `not too late` MEANS
            NOT ((`the last day for my proceedings, after an offer on` `the day of the statutory offer` `made` `I made a counter offer within 21 days` `on` `the day of my counter offer`) `is before` `the day I would commence`)

@export May I commence my court proceedings for damages on this day (s 134AB(12), (14), (20A))?
GIVEN `a conference was held or begun within 21 days after the response date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and WorkSafe or the self-insurer held or began a conference within 21 days after your response date
      `the day of the statutory offer` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer made its statutory offer (or the 60th day after the response date, if it made none)
      `I made a counter offer within 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a written statutory counter offer within 21 days after the statutory offer
      `the day of my counter offer` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your counter offer (any day if you made none)
      `the insurer accepted my counter offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer accepted your counter offer within 21 days
      `the Authority consented under s 134AB(20A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has consented under s 134AB(20A) to proceedings earlier or later than the usual window
      `the day I would commence` IS A DATE @desc The day you would commence the proceedings
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I commence my proceedings on this day` MEANS
    `I may commence proceedings, conference` `a conference was held or begun within 21 days after the response date` `offer on` `the day of the statutory offer` `counter offer` `I made a counter offer within 21 days` `on` `the day of my counter offer` `accepted` `the insurer accepted my counter offer` `consent` `the Authority consented under s 134AB(20A)` `commencing on` `the day I would commence`

@export What is the last day I may commence my court proceedings, without the Authority's consent (s 134AB(12)(e), (14))?
GIVEN `the day of the statutory offer` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer made its statutory offer (or is taken to have made it)
      `I made a counter offer within 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a written statutory counter offer within 21 days after the statutory offer
      `the day of my counter offer` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your counter offer (any day if you made none)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I may commence my proceedings` MEANS
    `the last day for my proceedings, after an offer on` `the day of the statutory offer` `made` `I made a counter offer within 21 days` `on` `the day of my counter offer`

§§ `s 134AB(15)-(17), (21A) -- what I may sue for`

-- s 134AB(16): with an assessment under 30%, no proceedings "unless -- (a) the Authority or self-insurer -- (i) is satisfied
-- that the injury is a serious injury; and (ii) issues to the worker a certificate ...; or (b) a court ... gives leave".
-- (17): "a worker who satisfies subparagraph (i) of subsection (38)(b) but not subparagraph (ii) of that subsection, is
-- entitled to bring proceedings in accordance with subsection (16)(b) for the recovery of damages for pain and suffering
-- only." (21A): a worker who failed on leave and then obtains 30% or more "is not entitled to recover damages for the same
-- relevant injury". (9), (15): a deemed serious injury.
-- READING (fork F11): (17) is read for a certificate under (16)(a) as for leave under (16)(b) ("For the purposes of
-- paragraphs (a) and (b) of subsection (16)").
DECLARE `What I may sue for` IS ONE OF
    `pecuniary loss damages and pain and suffering damages`
    `pain and suffering damages only`
    `no proceedings yet`
    `no damages for this injury`

DECLARE `Serious injury grounds` IS ONE OF
    `both the pain and suffering and the loss of earning capacity consequences`
    `the pain and suffering consequence only`

GIVEN `my injury is deemed serious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a certificate under s 134AB(16)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gave me leave under s 134AB(16)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grounds` IS A `Serious injury grounds`
      `I failed on leave and later obtained 30% or more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What I may sue for`
`what I may sue for under s 134AB, deemed` `my injury is deemed serious` `certificate` `I have a certificate under s 134AB(16)(a)` `leave` `the court gave me leave under s 134AB(16)(b)` `on` `the grounds` `(21A)` `I failed on leave and later obtained 30% or more` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I failed on leave and later obtained 30% or more` THEN `no damages for this injury`
           IF `my injury is deemed serious` THEN `pecuniary loss damages and pain and suffering damages`
           IF `I have a certificate under s 134AB(16)(a)` OR `the court gave me leave under s 134AB(16)(b)` THEN `by the grounds`
           OTHERWISE `no proceedings yet`
    WHERE
        `by the grounds` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the grounds`
            WHEN `both the pain and suffering and the loss of earning capacity consequences` THEN `pecuniary loss damages and pain and suffering damages`
            WHEN `the pain and suffering consequence only` THEN `pain and suffering damages only`

@export What damages may I sue for under s 134AB (s 134AB(9), (15), (16), (17), (21A))?
GIVEN `my injury is deemed serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury is deemed serious: an impairment of 30% or more assessed under s 104B before your application, or no answer from WorkSafe in time
      `I have a certificate under s 134AB(16)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer, satisfied your injury is serious, has issued you a certificate consenting to proceedings
      `the court gave me leave under s 134AB(16)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court (not the Magistrates' Court) has given you leave to bring proceedings
      `the grounds` IS A `Serious injury grounds` @desc On what the certificate or leave rests: both the pain and suffering and the loss of earning capacity consequences, or the pain and suffering consequence only
      `I failed on leave and later obtained 30% or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court refused you leave and you later obtained an impairment determination of 30% or more under s 104B for the same injury
GIVETH A `What I may sue for`
`What damages may I sue for under s 134AB` MEANS
    `what I may sue for under s 134AB, deemed` `my injury is deemed serious` `certificate` `I have a certificate under s 134AB(16)(a)` `leave` `the court gave me leave under s 134AB(16)(b)` `on` `the grounds` `(21A)` `I failed on leave and later obtained 30% or more`

§§ `s 134AB(38)(e)-(g) -- the loss of earning capacity test`

-- s 134AB(38)(e): no certificate or leave on the loss of earning capacity ground "unless the worker establishes ... that --
-- (i) at the date of a decision under subsection (16)(a) or at the date of the hearing ..., the worker has a loss of earning
-- capacity of 40 per centum or more, measured (except in the case of a worker referred to in item 1 of Schedule 1A or a
-- worker under the age of 26 years at the date of the injury) as set out in paragraph (f); and (ii) the worker ... will
-- after the date of the decision or of the hearing continue permanently to have a loss of earning capacity which will be
-- productive of financial loss of 40 per centum or more". (f): compare "(i) the worker's gross income from personal exertion
-- (expressed at an annual rate) which the worker is -- (A) earning, whether in suitable employment or not; or (B) capable of
-- earning in suitable employment -- as at that date, whichever is the greater, and -- (ii) the gross income (expressed at an
-- annual rate) that the worker was earning or was capable of earning ... during that part of the period within 3 years
-- before and 3 years after the injury as most fairly reflects the worker's earning capacity had the injury not occurred".
-- (g): no such loss "where the worker has, or would have after rehabilitation or retraining, ... a capacity for any
-- employment ... which, if exercised, would result in the worker earning more than 60 per centum of gross income from
-- personal exertion as determined in accordance with paragraph (f) had the injury not occurred".
-- For a worker under 26 at the injury, or in Schedule 1A item 1, (f) does not measure (i): the percentage found is asked.
-- (ii) is a finding about the future: asked. "shall not grant ... unless": JUST FALSE when the test fails.
GIVEN `the income I am earning a year` IS A NUMBER
      `the income I could earn a year in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the income I would have had a year without the injury` IS A NUMBER
      `I was under 26 at the injury or am a Schedule 1A item 1 worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss of earning capacity found for me` IS A NUMBER
      `my loss will permanently be 40% or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the most I could earn a year after rehabilitation in any employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`I meet the loss of earning capacity test, earning` `the income I am earning a year` `capable of` `the income I could earn a year in suitable employment` `against` `the income I would have had a year without the injury` `young` `I was under 26 at the injury or am a Schedule 1A item 1 worker` `found` `the loss of earning capacity found for me` `permanent` `my loss will permanently be 40% or more` `after rehabilitation` `the most I could earn a year after rehabilitation in any employment` MEANS
    IF `the income I would have had a year without the injury` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: no pre-injury income to measure a loss against)
    ELSE JUST (`(e)(i)` AND `my loss will permanently be 40% or more` AND (NOT `(g) bars it`))
    WHERE
        `the greater now` MEANS max `the income I am earning a year` `the income I could earn a year in suitable employment`
        `the measured loss` MEANS ((`the income I would have had a year without the injury` MINUS `the greater now`) DIVIDED BY `the income I would have had a year without the injury`) TIMES 100
        `(e)(i)` MEANS
            IF `I was under 26 at the injury or am a Schedule 1A item 1 worker`
            THEN `the loss of earning capacity found for me` AT LEAST 40
            ELSE `the measured loss` AT LEAST 40
        `(g) bars it` MEANS `the most I could earn a year after rehabilitation in any employment` GREATER THAN (`the income I would have had a year without the injury` TIMES 0.6)

@export Do I meet the 40% loss of earning capacity test for a serious injury certificate or leave (s 134AB(38)(e)-(g))?
GIVEN `the income I am earning a year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross income from personal exertion now, at an annual rate, in dollars
      `the income I could earn a year in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross income you are capable of earning now in suitable employment, at an annual rate, in dollars
      `the income I would have had a year without the injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross annual income that most fairly reflects your earning capacity had the injury not occurred, from the 3 years before and after it, in dollars
      `I was under 26 at the injury or am a Schedule 1A item 1 worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 26 when injured, or are a worker in item 1 of Schedule 1A
      `the loss of earning capacity found for me` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if you were under 26 or are a Schedule 1A item 1 worker: the loss of earning capacity found for you, in per cent
      `my loss will permanently be 40% or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will continue permanently to have a loss of earning capacity productive of financial loss of 40% or more
      `the most I could earn a year after rehabilitation in any employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The most you could earn a year in any employment, now or after rehabilitation or retraining, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I meet the loss of earning capacity test` MEANS
    `I meet the loss of earning capacity test, earning` `the income I am earning a year` `capable of` `the income I could earn a year in suitable employment` `against` `the income I would have had a year without the injury` `young` `I was under 26 at the injury or am a Schedule 1A item 1 worker` `found` `the loss of earning capacity found for me` `permanent` `my loss will permanently be 40% or more` `after rehabilitation` `the most I could earn a year after rehabilitation in any employment`

§ `Section 135A -- employment before 12 November 1997`

§§ `s 135A(2), (2A) and s 135AC -- may I recover damages`

-- s 135A(2): "A worker may recover damages ... (a) if employment of that nature was a significant contributing factor, and the
-- injury is a serious injury and arose on or after 1 December 1992; or (b) if the injury is a serious injury and arose
-- before that date but the incapacity arising from the injury did not become known until that date or a later date."
-- (2A): no proceedings "unless a determination of the degree of impairment of the worker has been made under subsection
-- (3)" (subject to (2D)). s 135AC: proceedings "must not be commenced -- (a) subject to the Limitation of Actions Act 1958,
-- unless paragraph (b) applies, unless an application for a determination ... under section 135A(2B) has been made ...
-- before 1 September 2000; or (b) if the cause of action arose before 12 November 1997 and the incapacity arising from the
-- injury was not known until after 12 November 1997, unless an application ... has been made ... before the expiration of 3
-- years after the date the incapacity became known."
-- READING (fork F12): the cause of action is taken to arise on the day of the injury (s 135AD keeps the Limitation of
-- Actions Act's accrual rules; the deposit does not hold them).
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `my injury is a serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employment was a significant contributing factor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day my incapacity became known` IS A DATE
      `a determination under s 135A(3) has been made or I am deemed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied for a determination under s 135A(2B)` IS A DATE
      `the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 still allows my proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`I may recover damages under s 135A, injured on` `the day of the injury` `serious` `my injury is a serious injury` `significant` `employment was a significant contributing factor` `known on` `the day my incapacity became known` `determined` `a determination under s 135A(3) has been made or I am deemed` `applied on` `the day I applied for a determination under s 135A(2B)` `limitation` `the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 still allows my proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the day of the injury` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 12 11 1997)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 135A(1), employment before 12 November 1997)
    ELSE JUST (`(2) allows it` AND `a determination under s 135A(3) has been made or I am deemed` AND `s 135AC allows it`)
    WHERE
        `(2) allows it` MEANS
            IF `the day of the injury` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 1 12 1992)
            THEN `employment was a significant contributing factor` AND `my injury is a serious injury`
            ELSE `my injury is a serious injury` AND (`the day my incapacity became known` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 1 12 1992))
        `s 135AC allows it` MEANS
            IF `the day my incapacity became known` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 13 11 1997)
            THEN NOT ((`three years after` `the day my incapacity became known`) `is before` `the day I applied for a determination under s 135A(2B)`)
            ELSE `the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 still allows my proceedings` AND (`the day I applied for a determination under s 135A(2B)` `is before` (`the calendar date` 1 9 2000))

-- 3 years after a day: the same day of the month three years on. A period of 3 years "after" a day starts the next day
-- and expires at the end of that day three years on, so an application made on it is in time.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`three years after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 3)

@export May I recover damages for my pre-12 November 1997 work injury (s 135A(2), (2A), s 135AC)?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of your injury (from employment before 12 November 1997)
      `my injury is a serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury is a serious injury: determined at 30% or more, deemed, certified by WorkSafe or the self-insurer, or found by the court on leave
      `employment was a significant contributing factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether employment of that nature was a significant contributing factor to the injury
      `the day my incapacity became known` IS A DATE @desc The day the incapacity arising from the injury became known
      `a determination under s 135A(3) has been made or I am deemed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer has determined your degree of impairment under s 135A(3), or you are deemed to have a serious injury because it did not answer in time
      `the day I applied for a determination under s 135A(2B)` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied in writing for that determination
      `the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 still allows my proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 still allows your proceedings (it matters if your incapacity was known by 12 November 1997)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I recover damages under s 135A` MEANS
    `I may recover damages under s 135A, injured on` `the day of the injury` `serious` `my injury is a serious injury` `significant` `employment was a significant contributing factor` `known on` `the day my incapacity became known` `determined` `a determination under s 135A(3) has been made or I am deemed` `applied on` `the day I applied for a determination under s 135A(2B)` `limitation` `the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 still allows my proceedings`

§§ `s 135A(3), (2D), (2DB), (4)(b) -- a deemed serious injury, and the leave deadline`

-- s 135A(3): "If the Authority or self-insurer determines that the degree of impairment ... would, if assessed in accordance
-- with section 91 be 30 per centum or more, the injury is deemed to be a serious injury". (2DB), with (2AA) and (2BB), as
-- above: deemed if no advice within 120 days (210 for an application received from 11 to 31 August 2000), less the days of a
-- refused or hindered examination. Plain days.
GIVEN `a determination of 30% or more was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was received` IS A DATE
      `WorkSafe has advised me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the advice` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the days disregarded under s 135A(2BB)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`I am deemed to have a serious injury under s 135A, thirty per cent` `a determination of 30% or more was made` `received` `the day the application was received` `advised` `WorkSafe has advised me` `on` `the day of the advice` `as of` `today` `disregarded` `the days disregarded under s 135A(2BB)` MEANS
    IF `a determination of 30% or more was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST (`deemed serious, if` (`what became of` (`s 135A(2D) -- the Authority or self-insurer must advise the worker within the days allowed` `the days allowed`) `with` `advise the worker in writing of the impairment determination or the refusal to make one` `done` `WorkSafe has advised me` `at` (`plain` `the day of the advice`) `now` (`plain` `today`)))
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS
            IF `the day the application was received` `falls from` (`the calendar date` 11 8 2000) `to` (`the calendar date` 31 8 2000)
            THEN 210
            ELSE 120
        GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `plain` `the day` MEANS max 0 ((`the plain days from` `the day the application was received` `to` `the day`) MINUS `the days disregarded under s 135A(2BB)`)

@export Am I deemed to have a serious injury under s 135A (a determination of 30% or more, or no answer within 120 days: s 135A(3), (2DB))?
GIVEN `a determination of 30% or more was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer has determined your degree of impairment under s 135A(3) at 30% or more
      `the day the application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer received your written application for a determination under s 135A(2B)
      `WorkSafe has advised me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer has advised you in writing of the determination or of a refusal to make one
      `the day of the advice` IS A DATE @desc The day of that advice (any day if there has been none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `the days disregarded under s 135A(2BB)` IS A NUMBER @desc Days that do not count because you unreasonably refused or hindered a requested medical examination (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I deemed to have a serious injury under s 135A` MEANS
    `I am deemed to have a serious injury under s 135A, thirty per cent` `a determination of 30% or more was made` `received` `the day the application was received` `advised` `WorkSafe has advised me` `on` `the day of the advice` `as of` `today` `disregarded` `the days disregarded under s 135A(2BB)`

-- s 135A(4)(b): leave of a court "on the application of the worker made within 30 days after the determination was made or,
-- with the consent of the Authority under subsection (6A), after that period". Plain days.
@export By when must I apply to the court for leave to sue under s 135A, if my impairment was determined under 30% (s 135A(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the determination was made` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer made its determination of your degree of impairment under s 135A(3)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for leave to sue under s 135A` MEANS `the date` 30 `plain days after` `the day the determination was made`

§ `What the court can award, and what follows (ss 134AB, 135A)`

§§ `s 134AB(22), s 135A(7) -- thresholds and maximums`

-- s 134AB(22): "A court must not ... award to a worker in respect of an injury -- (a) pecuniary loss damages -- (i) if the
-- total pecuniary loss damages assessed, before the reduction (if any) under section 26(1) of the Wrongs Act 1958 and before
-- the reduction (if any) under subsection (25), is less than $56 650 or that amount as varied ... as at the date of the
-- award; or (ii) in excess of $1 275 570 or that amount as varied ...; (b) pain and suffering damages -- (i) [below] $54
-- 730 ...; or (ii) in excess of $555 350 ...; or (c) damages of any other kind, other than damages in the nature of
-- interest." s 135A(7): the same, with $59 670, $1 343 540, $50 680 and $514 360, and the reduction under (11).
-- READING (fork F13): the maximum caps the damages assessed; the reductions of (25) and the Wrongs Act follow.
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Damages section`
      `the head` IS A `Head of damages`
      `the damages assessed` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most the court may award under` `the section` `for` `the head` `on an assessment of` `the damages assessed` `on` `the day of the award` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the damages limits under` `the section` `for` `the head` `on` `the day of the award`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the varied amounts for that year are not deposited)
    WHEN JUST `the limits` THEN
        IF `the damages assessed` LESS THAN `the limits`'s `the threshold`
        THEN JUST 0
        ELSE JUST (min `the damages assessed` (`the limits`'s `the maximum`))

@export What can the court award me for pecuniary loss or for pain and suffering, given the thresholds and maximums (s 134AB(22), s 135A(7))?
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Damages section` @desc The section your claim is under: section 134AB (injuries from 20 October 1999) or section 135A (before 12 November 1997)
      `the head` IS A `Head of damages` @desc Pecuniary loss damages (loss of earnings or earning capacity) or pain and suffering damages
      `the damages assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages assessed for that head, before any reduction for compensation paid or contributory negligence, in dollars
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE @desc The day of the award (amounts are known for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What can the court award me for this head of damages` MEANS
    `the most the court may award under` `the section` `for` `the head` `on an assessment of` `the damages assessed` `on` `the day of the award`

§§ `s 134AB(25), (26), s 135A(11), (12) -- the reductions`

-- s 134AB(25): the judgment "must be reduced by -- (a) to the extent that it is in respect of pecuniary loss, the amount of
-- compensation (if any) paid otherwise than under section 98C, 98E and Division 2B of Part IV [medical and like services] ...;
-- (b) to the extent that it is in respect of non-pecuniary loss, the amount of compensation (if any) paid under section 98C
-- and 98E." (26): that reduction "must be made before the reduction (if any) under section 26(1) of the Wrongs Act 1958".
-- s 135A(11), (12): the same, with sections 98 and 98A.
-- The Wrongs Act reduction (contributory negligence) is a borrowed rule: its percentage is asked. The transport accident
-- exception in (25)(a) is not encoded.
-- READING (fork F14): each head is reduced to no less than nothing.
GIVEN `the pecuniary loss damages awarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the pain and suffering damages awarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation paid that counts against pecuniary loss` IS A NUMBER
      `the impairment compensation paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributory negligence reduction in per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the judgment after the reductions, pecuniary` `the pecuniary loss damages awarded` `pain and suffering` `the pain and suffering damages awarded` `less` `the compensation paid that counts against pecuniary loss` `and` `the impairment compensation paid` `contributory` `the contributory negligence reduction in per cent` MEANS
    (`after (25)` PLUS `after (25) for pain and suffering`) TIMES ((100 MINUS `the contributory negligence reduction in per cent`) DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHERE
        `after (25)` MEANS max 0 (`the pecuniary loss damages awarded` MINUS `the compensation paid that counts against pecuniary loss`)
        `after (25) for pain and suffering` MEANS max 0 (`the pain and suffering damages awarded` MINUS `the impairment compensation paid`)

@export How much will my damages judgment be after compensation already paid and contributory negligence are taken off (s 134AB(25), (26); s 135A(11), (12))?
GIVEN `the pecuniary loss damages awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The pecuniary loss damages the court may award you (after the threshold and maximum), in dollars
      `the pain and suffering damages awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The pain and suffering damages the court may award you (after the threshold and maximum), in dollars
      `the compensation paid that counts against pecuniary loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Compensation already paid to you other than impairment lump sums and medical and like services (mostly weekly payments), in dollars
      `the impairment compensation paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Impairment lump sums already paid to you (under s 98C and s 98E, or for a pre-1997 injury s 98 and s 98A), in dollars
      `the contributory negligence reduction in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The reduction for your own share of responsibility under s 26(1) of the Wrongs Act 1958, in per cent (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much will my damages judgment be after the reductions` MEANS
    `the judgment after the reductions, pecuniary` `the pecuniary loss damages awarded` `pain and suffering` `the pain and suffering damages awarded` `less` `the compensation paid that counts against pecuniary loss` `and` `the impairment compensation paid` `contributory` `the contributory negligence reduction in per cent`

§§ `s 134AB(28), (28A), s 135A(13A) -- who pays the costs`

-- s 134AB(28): in proceedings commenced after a statutory offer "(a) if no liability to pay damages is established, the worker
-- must pay the costs ... of the employer, Authority or self-insurer and the worker's own costs; (b) if judgment is obtained or a
-- settlement or compromise is made in an amount not less than 90 per cent of the worker's statutory counter offer ... and
-- more than the statutory offer ..., the Authority or self-insurer must pay the worker's costs ... and its own costs; (c) ...
-- in an amount not more than the statutory offer ..., the worker must pay the costs ... of the Authority or self-insurer and
-- the worker's own costs; (d) ... more than the statutory offer ... but less than 90 per cent of the worker's statutory
-- counter offer ..., each party bears its own costs". s 135A(13A): the same words.
-- s 134AB(28A), (28B): for this comparison the (25) reduction is "the amount of compensation paid -- (a) to the date of the
-- statutory counter offer ... or (b) to the date of the deemed statutory counter offer", made before the Wrongs Act
-- reduction. s 135A has no (28A): the amount is the judgment as entered (fork F15).
DECLARE `Costs outcome` IS ONE OF
    `I pay both sides' costs`
    `the Authority or self-insurer pays both sides' costs`
    `each side bears its own costs`

GIVEN `liability is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the judgment` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory offer` IS A NUMBER
      `my statutory counter offer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Costs outcome`
`the costs outcome, liability` `liability is established` `judgment of` `the amount of the judgment` `offer` `the statutory offer` `counter offer` `my statutory counter offer` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `liability is established`) THEN `I pay both sides' costs`
           IF `the amount of the judgment` AT MOST `the statutory offer` THEN `I pay both sides' costs`
           IF `the amount of the judgment` AT LEAST (`my statutory counter offer` TIMES 0.9) THEN `the Authority or self-insurer pays both sides' costs`
           OTHERWISE `each side bears its own costs`

@export Who pays the costs of my damages proceedings, comparing the judgment with the statutory offer and my counter offer (s 134AB(28), s 135A(13A))?
GIVEN `liability is established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a liability to pay you damages was established
      `the amount of the judgment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the judgment, settlement or compromise, in dollars (for s 134AB, after taking off compensation paid up to the counter offer and any contributory negligence reduction)
      `the statutory offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory offer made by WorkSafe or the self-insurer, in dollars (0 if it is taken to have offered nothing)
      `my statutory counter offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Your statutory counter offer, in dollars (or the maximum damages, if you are taken to have made one)
GIVETH A `Costs outcome`
`Who pays the costs of my damages proceedings` MEANS
    `the costs outcome, liability` `liability is established` `judgment of` `the amount of the judgment` `offer` `the statutory offer` `counter offer` `my statutory counter offer`

-- s 134AB(28A): the amount the costs rule compares, from the damages awarded.
@export What amount is compared with the offers for costs under s 134AB(28), after s 134AB(28A) and (28B)?
GIVEN `the damages awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages the court awards you (after the thresholds and maximums), in dollars
      `the compensation paid up to the counter offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensation that counts against the damages, paid up to the day of your counter offer (or of the deemed counter offer), in dollars
      `the contributory negligence reduction in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The reduction for your own share of responsibility under s 26(1) of the Wrongs Act 1958, in per cent (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What amount is compared with the offers for costs` MEANS
    (max 0 (`the damages awarded` MINUS `the compensation paid up to the counter offer`)) TIMES ((100 MINUS `the contributory negligence reduction in per cent`) DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `s 134AB(32), s 135A(14) -- the discount rate`

-- s 134AB(32): the present value of future loss "must be qualified by adopting a discount rate of 6 per centum"; s 135A(14):
-- "a discount rate of 3 per centum".
@export What discount rate is used to work out the lump sum for my future loss (s 134AB(32), s 135A(14))?
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Damages section` @desc The section your claim is under: section 134AB or section 135A
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What discount rate applies to my future loss` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 134AB` THEN 6
    WHEN `section 135A` THEN 3

§§ `s 134AB(36)-(36C), s 135A(18)-(18AC) -- what my damages do to my compensation`

-- s 134AB(36): after judgment, compromise or settlement the Authority, employer or self-insurer "is not liable -- (a) where
-- pecuniary loss damages are awarded, to pay weekly payments in respect of the injury; or (b) where pain and suffering damages
-- are awarded, to make payments under section 98C or 98E". (36A): if the worker "was, at the date of the judgment,
-- compromise or settlement, still in receipt of compensation in the form of weekly payments, where pecuniary loss damages are
-- awarded against the Authority, employer or self-insurer, [it] must, until the date on which payment is issued to a worker
-- for the purpose of payment of the judgment ..., pay to the worker a weekly amount equal to the net weekly amount that, but
-- for subsection (36), would have been payable". (36B): "only ... against a sole defendant where that sole defendant was the
-- worker's employer at the date of the injury". s 135A(18)-(18AB): the same, with sections 98 and 98A.
DECLARE `My weekly payments after damages` IS ONE OF
    `my weekly payments are not affected`
    `my weekly payments stop`
    `a weekly amount continues until payment of the judgment is issued, then stops`

GIVEN `pecuniary loss damages were awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was still receiving weekly payments at the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only defendant was my employer at the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment of the judgment has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My weekly payments after damages`
`my weekly payments after damages, pecuniary` `pecuniary loss damages were awarded` `receiving` `I was still receiving weekly payments at the judgment` `sole employer` `the only defendant was my employer at the injury` `paid` `payment of the judgment has been issued` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `pecuniary loss damages were awarded`) THEN `my weekly payments are not affected`
           IF `I was still receiving weekly payments at the judgment` AND `the only defendant was my employer at the injury` AND (NOT `payment of the judgment has been issued`) THEN `a weekly amount continues until payment of the judgment is issued, then stops`
           OTHERWISE `my weekly payments stop`

@export Do my weekly payments stop after my damages judgment or settlement (s 134AB(36)-(36B), s 135A(18)-(18AB))?
GIVEN `pecuniary loss damages were awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment, settlement or compromise includes pecuniary loss damages
      `I was still receiving weekly payments at the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were still receiving weekly payments on the date of the judgment, settlement or compromise
      `the only defendant was my employer at the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only defendant was the employer you worked for when injured
      `payment of the judgment has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether payment of the judgment, settlement or compromise has been issued to you
GIVETH A `My weekly payments after damages`
`Do my weekly payments stop after my damages` MEANS
    `my weekly payments after damages, pecuniary` `pecuniary loss damages were awarded` `receiving` `I was still receiving weekly payments at the judgment` `sole employer` `the only defendant was my employer at the injury` `paid` `payment of the judgment has been issued`

@export Do my impairment lump sum payments stop because I was awarded pain and suffering damages (s 134AB(36)(b), s 135A(18)(b))?
GIVEN `pain and suffering damages were awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment, settlement or compromise includes pain and suffering damages
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do my impairment payments stop after my damages` MEANS JUST `pain and suffering damages were awarded`
